<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mustafa Khan of Shirvan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1792–1820</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mustafa Khan was the last khan of Shirvan, ruling from 1792. He reunited the khanate after a period of domination by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quba">Quba</a> and built a mountain stronghold at Fit-dagh, balancing between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. He accepted Russian protection in 1805 but remained restless, and in 1820 he fled to Persia, after which Russia annexed the khanate.</p></div>
